# ── Local Firebase project override ─────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in to point THIS machine's dev
# server at a scratch Firebase project instead of the live tournament.
#
# Why you want this: the admin console writes to Firestore as you edit, so a dev
# server aimed at production can corrupt a real round with one stray click.
# There is one Firebase project behind this app and it holds the real
# tournament.
#
# Leave every line below unset (or delete .env.local) to use production —
# that's the default and what Vercel builds use.
#
# Values come from the Firebase console: Project settings → General → Your apps
# → SDK setup and configuration. Create a fresh project (e.g. "wbc-dev"), add a
# Web app, then deploy the shared rules to it:
#
#   firebase use <your-dev-project-id> && firebase deploy --only firestore:rules
#
# All six are required together; setting only some throws at startup. That is
# deliberate — a half-applied override would pair a dev project id with the
# production API key, look like it worked, and write to production anyway.

# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# ── A note on authDomain ────────────────────────────────────────────
# In production this is wannabecup.com rather than the default
# wannabecup-c5aab.firebaseapp.com (once AUTH_PROVIDERS_ENABLED is on), so the
# signInWithRedirect flow stays first-party inside the installed PWA — see the
# comment on PROD_FIREBASE_CONFIG in src/firebase.js.
#
# A scratch project has no such domain and no Vercel rewrite in front of it, so
# set VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN to that project's own
# <project-id>.firebaseapp.com. The override replaces authDomain along with
# everything else and does NOT inherit the wannabecup.com switch, which is
# correct: that domain only resolves because of THIS project's rewrites.
#
# The scratch project also needs its own sign-in providers enabled
# (Authentication → Sign-in method) and localhost added under Authorized
# domains, or the dev server can read data but nobody can log into it.

# ── Push notifications ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The service worker (public/firebase-messaging-sw.js) is a STATIC file and
# cannot read env vars — it carries the production Firebase config inline. A
# dev server pointed at a scratch project therefore gets no web push at all,
# which is the safe direction to fail.

# ── Serverless API secrets (api/*.js) ───────────────────────────────
# Only needed if you run `vercel dev` — i.e. only if you are changing the
# handler in api/ itself. In production this is set in the Vercel project.
# Never commit a real value.

# RAPIDAPI_KEY=

# ── Which tournament the app opens on ───────────────────────────────
# The live tournament is named in src/lib/editionHome.js (wbc_2026). Set this
# to point a build somewhere else — next year's tournament once it is the one
# being played, or the sandbox for a store build handed to testers:
#
#   VITE_DEFAULT_EDITION=wbc_2027
#
# It decides two things: which edition a device with no pointer opens on, and
# where "Back to …" in the edition banner goes. A device that has switched
# years keeps its own pointer for as long as the app stays open — see
# lib/editionHome.

# VITE_DEFAULT_EDITION=
